@startuml
title LMS v1.0 — UML Deployment Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle uml2

actor Student
actor Lecturer
actor "Head of Department" as HOD
actor Administrator as Admin

node "School workstation\n(single Windows PC)" <<device>> as PC {
  node "Windows 10/11" <<executionEnvironment>> as Windows {
    node "MSYS2 UCRT64 runtime\n(or packaged equivalent)" <<executionEnvironment>> as Runtime {
      artifact "lms_gui.exe\nQt 6 desktop application" as App
      artifact "Qt 6 Widgets runtime" as Qt
      artifact "SQLite 3 runtime" as SQLite
      artifact "Argon2 runtime" as Argon2
      artifact "UCRT runtime libraries" as UCRT
    }

    database "lms.db\nSQLite database\nC:\\SchoolLMS\\lms.db" as DB
    artifact "Assignment files\nuser-selected local paths" as Files
  }
}

Student --> App : signs in and uses student workspace
Lecturer --> App : signs in and uses lecturer workspace
HOD --> App : signs in and uses HOD workspace
Admin --> App : signs in and uses administration workspace

App --> Qt : GUI
App --> SQLite : database driver
App --> Argon2 : password hashing
App --> UCRT : native runtime
App --> DB : local SQLite file access
App --> Files : stores/resolves file references

note right of PC
  This release is a desktop application,
  not a client/server deployment.
  The roles use the application on this PC.
  SQLite and submitted files are local;
  files are not uploaded or synchronized.
end note

note bottom of DB
  Includes the per-student extensions table
  and the v1.1 assignment class extensions table.
  On first launch the schema can be created,
  but the database has no initial user.
  Secure first-administrator provisioning
  is required before operational use.
end note

@enduml
